{
  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 with multiprofile achieves ~0.65 acc (configs 005/006), far exceeding pca_n2000 singleprofile (0.485) and scgpt singleprofile (0.411). For pca_n2000, multiprofile+avgpool gave a ~0.106 boost over singleprofile, but we have no data on whether scvi_n200 benefits similarly from multiprofile or is already strong in singleprofile. Question: config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) isolates the profile-setting effect for the best-performing RNA encoder with only one variable changed relative to configs 005/006. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) It is a clean single-factor comparison that directly tests whether the multiprofile gain is encoder-dependent or universal. (2) The result determines whether future multimodal experiments should use multiprofile or singleprofile for scvi_n200, saving budget by avoiding redundant variants. (3) It is lower-risk and more interpretable than jumping to a multimodal config where multiple new factors (image encoder, fusion strategy) would confound the result. (4) If scvi_n200 singleprofile is already competitive (~0.60+), it shifts focus toward fusion/image questions; if it drops substantially, it confirms multiprofile is essential and narrows the search space."
}

